{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.KashaevDensityEqualsSdpMultiplicity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.KashaevDensityEqualsSdpMultiplicity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Kashaev.kashaev_density_eq_sdp_multiplicity_satisfiable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Kashaev.kashaev_density_eq_sdp_multiplicity_satisfiable","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/kashaev-density-equals-sdp-multiplicity.lean#L195-L212","doc":"…and the class is not refutable *vacuously*: it has a model, so it is a genuine\nconstraint rather than a contradiction that every parameter tuple falsifies. Refutability\nalone would not distinguish those two, and a contradictory hypothesis class would make every\ndownstream conditional result vacuously true — the failure mode this rewrite exists to remove,\nwearing the opposite sign.\n\n**This is emphatically NOT a witness for the conjecture**, and it is deliberately a `theorem`\nrather than an `instance` so that instance search can never find it. The tuple is a toy:\n`Atom = Unit`, `m_e` and `Vol` normalised to `1`, and the prefactor set to the integer `2` by\nhand. Nothing here computes a `ν_SDP` from an SDP, which is the open half (see the header). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Kashaev.kashaev_density_eq_sdp_multiplicity_refutable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Kashaev.kashaev_density_eq_sdp_multiplicity_refutable","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/kashaev-density-equals-sdp-multiplicity.lean#L180-L193","doc":"The class is **refutable**, which the previous `holds : Prop` carrier was not.\n\nThe refuting instantiation is the `⁴He` datum in miniature: `ρ_F = 1889/1000`, with `m_e` and\n`Vol` normalised to `1` and `B_pred` chosen so that `binding_formula`, `mE_pos` and `vol_pos`\nall *hold*. So the class fails on `identity` **alone** — the prefactor's non-integrality, not\nan inconsistent binding, is what refutes it, and it does so for every `ν_SDP` whatsoever.\n\nStated as a `theorem` rather than left implicit because \"the carrier asserts something\" is\nexactly the property that was missing, and a reader should be able to see it discharged rather\nthan take the docstring's word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Kashaev.not_of_prefactor_strictly_between","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Kashaev.not_of_prefactor_strictly_between","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/kashaev-density-equals-sdp-multiplicity.lean#L162-L178","doc":"A prefactor strictly between two consecutive naturals refutes the class, because\n`identity` forces the prefactor to be a natural-number cast.\n\nThis is the block's own `⁴He` negative, stated as a Lean obstruction: the AME2020-pinned\nprefactor there is `B_AME / (m_e · A · 8G) = 28.295673 / (0.51099895 · 4 · 8G) = 1.88917`\n([`he4_nu_sdp_binding_arbiter.py`](../../../computations/probes/he4_nu_sdp_binding_arbiter.py)),\nwhich lies strictly between `1` and `2` — so **no** choice of `ν_SDP` satisfies the identity\nat the doubly-magic point, and rounding `1.889 → 2` is a choice with no derived origin. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Kashaev.KashaevDensityEqualsSdpMultiplicity.binding_formula","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Kashaev.KashaevDensityEqualsSdpMultiplicity.binding_formula","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/kashaev-density-equals-sdp-multiplicity.lean#L160-L160","doc":"**The formula the identity feeds**, in the producer's form:\n`B_pred(K_w) = ρ_F · m_e · Vol_hyp(K_w)`. The magic-`A` closure is the same product with\n`vol a := A · 8G`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Kashaev.KashaevDensityEqualsSdpMultiplicity.identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Kashaev.KashaevDensityEqualsSdpMultiplicity.identity","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/kashaev-density-equals-sdp-multiplicity.lean#L156-L156","doc":"**The content.** `ρ_F(K_w) = ν_SDP(K_w)` — the prefactor is that integer exactly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Kashaev.KashaevDensityEqualsSdpMultiplicity.nuSdp_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Kashaev.KashaevDensityEqualsSdpMultiplicity.nuSdp_pos","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/kashaev-density-equals-sdp-multiplicity.lean#L154-L154","doc":"`ν_SDP` is a **strictly positive** integer multiplicity — `ℤ_{>0}` in the block, not\n`ℤ_{≥0}`. The strictness carries content: without it `ν_SDP ≡ 0` satisfies the identity for\nany zero prefactor and the class is back where it started. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Kashaev.KashaevDensityEqualsSdpMultiplicity.vol_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Kashaev.KashaevDensityEqualsSdpMultiplicity.vol_pos","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/kashaev-density-equals-sdp-multiplicity.lean#L150-L150","doc":"Scope: the atoms carrying a *hyperbolic* census knot. This is what excludes the\ndeuteron under owner ruling A of 2026-08-29 (`Vol = 0` for the canonical braid closure);\nsee the header. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Kashaev.KashaevDensityEqualsSdpMultiplicity.mE_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Kashaev.KashaevDensityEqualsSdpMultiplicity.mE_pos","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/kashaev-density-equals-sdp-multiplicity.lean#L146-L146","doc":"The electron mass scale is a genuine scale (CAL-1 is positive). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Kashaev.KashaevDensityEqualsSdpMultiplicity.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Kashaev.KashaevDensityEqualsSdpMultiplicity.mk","kind":"ctor","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/kashaev-density-equals-sdp-multiplicity.lean#L142-L142","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Kashaev.KashaevDensityEqualsSdpMultiplicity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Kashaev.KashaevDensityEqualsSdpMultiplicity","kind":"class","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/kashaev-density-equals-sdp-multiplicity.lean#L127-L160","doc":"**CONJECTURE.** The Kashaev density prefactor equals the joint-tower SDP Wedderburn\nmultiplicity: `ρ_F = ν_SDP ∈ ℤ_{>0}`, and the predicted binding is that integer multiple of\n`m_e · Vol_hyp`.\n\n`Atom` indexes the census atoms; `rhoF`, `nuSdp`, `bindingPred`, `vol` and `mE` are all\nsupplied **by the caller**, so the class is false at values that violate its fields — which is\nthe point (see the header). `nuSdp` is a bare `ℕ`-valued parameter and is **not** claimed to\nbe any SDP construct; the corpus has no type for the saturating projection whose dimension it\nis meant to be.\n\n**No instance is provided.** Downstream results consume this as\n`[KashaevDensityEqualsSdpMultiplicity Atom rhoF nuSdp bindingPred vol mE]` and are genuinely\nconditional on it.\n\n-- Ref: [leitner2026] conj:kashaev-density-equals-sdp-multiplicity ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:kashaev-density-equals-sdp-multiplicity","label":"conj:kashaev-density-equals-sdp-multiplicity","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/kashaev-density-equals-sdp-multiplicity.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}